{
  "$comment": [
    "The four dataset shapes PRD 8.1 enumerates, as one artefact per kind.",
    "",
    "Each declares the content hash of its own items. The hashes are not decoration: loadDataset",
    "recomputes them and refuses a file whose labels have moved without its version moving, which",
    "is the first of the two ways PRD 8.1 says an improvement gets faked.",
    "",
    "corpusSnapshot is the sha256 of the empty string throughout. These fixtures are labelled",
    "against no corpus — they exist to exercise the metrics, not to measure a system — and using a",
    "recognisable placeholder is more honest than inventing a digest that looks like a real",
    "snapshot somebody could go looking for.",
    "",
    "Each set carries a held-out item, so the seal has something to refuse."
  ],

